{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/pulls/1980","id":4393790550,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABBePsVg","html_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/pull/1980","diff_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/pull/1980.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ERCs/pull/1980.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/issues/1980","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/pulls/1980/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/pulls/1980/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/issues/1980/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/statuses/7a9e63a80bce04db53c6550103c1d41eca35f3d1","number":1980,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add ERC: Recomputable Verification Receipts","user":{"login":"pipavlo82","id":212635108,"node_id":"U_kgDODKyN5A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/212635108?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nERC-8404 proposes Recomputable Verification Receipts (RVR): a six-field, content-addressed receipt format for independently recomputing profile-defined verification results.\n\nRVR separates two axes:\n\n- verification outcome: `VERIFIED`, `REFUTED`, or `UNVERIFIABLE`;\n- recomputation status: `REPRODUCED`, `DIVERGED`, or `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE`.\n\nThe ERC defines the receipt fields, Verification Profile authority, evidence closure, canonical byte and digest rules, canonical-result projection checks, deterministic recomputation requirements, and mechanically distinct failure paths. Producer implementations are not authoritative; profile identity and exact committed contracts are.\n\n## Review status\n\nERC-8404 is assigned as a Standards Track ERC with status `Draft`. This pull request is open, Ready for Review, and awaiting editor review. The corresponding Ethereum Magicians discussion is:\n\nhttps://ethereum-magicians.org/t/erc-8404-recomputable-verification-receipts/29521\n\nReview is requested specifically for substantive issues concerning:\n\n- the six-field receipt surface;\n- the profile-bound recomputation target;\n- evidence and dependency closure;\n- canonical identity and hash-before-parse rules;\n- the separation of semantic outcome from recomputation status;\n- security boundaries and material overlap with neighboring proposals.\n\nExisting implementations and external profiles are conformance evidence, not normative dependencies of the generic RVR core.\n\n## Implementation evidence\n\nThe generic core has executable Python and TypeScript conformance implementations, an independent non-normative Rust reviewer, canonical-byte vectors, semantic negative controls, and external integration profiles. These artifacts remain outside the normative dependency surface of this proposal.\n\n## Numbering and CI\n\nAn editor assigned number 8404. The proposal is now `ERCS/erc-8404.md`, its front matter contains `eip: 8404`, and the current CI checks pass.\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nSpecial thanks to Tiago Merlini, Fede / Baby Blue Viper, Faisal Firdani, and Damon Zwicker for independent review, executable counterexamples, external integration work, and semantic boundary analysis that materially improved the draft.\n","labels":[{"id":6129127607,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABbVMQtw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/labels/t-erc","name":"t-erc","description":"","color":"FEF2C0","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6129463609,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABbVgxOQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/labels/s-draft","name":"s-draft","description":"","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6130026993,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABbWDJ8Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/labels/c-new","name":"c-new","description":"","color":"c5def5","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6138285773,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABbd7OzQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/labels/e-consensus","name":"e-consensus","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6138322754,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJvfjJM8AAAABbd9fQg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ERCs/labels/e-review","name":"e-review","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-29T23:51:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T17:14:02Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b27aba8da09e95e892cf7bd857c413c404c1440d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"eip-review-bot","id":128646734,"node_id":"U_kgDOB6r-Tg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128646734?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eip-review-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/eip-review-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eip-review-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eip-review-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ei